      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SECRET STORY (1) settled back off the inside but went through his gears strongly to find the frame with a 7 length second (22.11) at Q Lakeside in Grade 5. Rarely misses off this draw. Has a very good strike-rate from this draw, with three wins from four starts. Makes plenty of appeal. HARA'S PUMPKIN (6) missed the frame latest when fifth at Q Lakeside (25.95) but was a winner four back in the best time of the program. Solid record here at this trip including nine wins. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Warrants plenty of respect. WALKING CARPET (3) is a capable type and proved too classy last time to win by 0.8 lengths at this track in a handy 19.94 beating Out Of Whiskey. One of the key runners again. OSCAR BRAVO (2) drops in journey and is not to be underestimated.",
